A command has string properties `commandId`, `type`, and `holdId`. A `hold` command additionally has a positive integer `seats` property. Apply these lifecycle rules:

- `hold` creates a new `ACTIVE` hold and subtracts its seats from availability. It must throw an `Error` if its `holdId` already exists or insufficient seats remain.
- `commit` changes an `ACTIVE` hold to `COMMITTED`; availability does not change.
- `cancel` changes an `ACTIVE` hold to `CANCELLED` and restores its seats.
- `commit` and `cancel` must throw an `Error` when the hold does not exist or is no longer `ACTIVE`.
- Unsupported command types must throw an `Error`.

